WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_devf_341'), 'At 14:12, 31% of checkout requests fail. You have saved the four pieces of evidence above. A teammate says the code diff of v3.2.0 is 1,400 lines and asks to keep v3.2.0 running "until we know exactly which line broke it". The previous release is recorded in the deploy log as checkout v3.1.4 (sha256:2b9a55...).

Statement: "Keeping v3.2.0 running until the broken line is found is the better choice, because rolling back would destroy the evidence needed to fix it."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Users are failing now, the previous version is known by digest, and rolling back is a one-minute traffic change. The evidence is already saved (logs, metrics, the deploy log), and the broken image still exists in the registry, so it can be run again in staging to debug. The order is: stop the damage (roll back), then find the cause, then fix and verify. Debugging in production while 31% of orders fail turns a 10-minute incident into an hour-long one.', 5, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_devf_341') AND order_index = 5)
    RETURNING id
)
