       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_fix_devf_342'), 2, 'Look at how config_problems decides that a variable is set, and at the first if in check_problems: which values of ok does a plain truth test accept? Also notice which parameter of check_problems is never used.'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_fix_devf_342'), 3, 'A similar check on different input: a disk check gets {"used_pct": "95"} and a limit of 90. `"   ".strip() == ""` is True, `bool("false")` is True, `isinstance(1, bool)` is False and `isinstance(False, bool)` is True. So the check first asks "is used_pct a number at all?" (otherwise "disk: invalid result"), and only then compares it with the limit, where exactly 90 still passes.');
